  <section|Scope and notation><label|scope-and-notation>

  The prose uses the shared entries in <hlink|<verbatim|blueprint/glossary.md>|../../glossary.tm>:
  <verbatim|G \<subset\> U(r_G)>, <verbatim|P_p>, <verbatim|D_N>,
  <verbatim|a_N=D_N^{-1}>, <verbatim|\\ell_{N,p}=P_pD_N>,
  <verbatim|\\beta_{N,p}>, and the public Wilson family <verbatim|\\mathcal
  W>. The local symbols <verbatim|\\ell>, <verbatim|\\Lambda_\\ell>,
  <verbatim|E_\\ell>, <verbatim|S_\\ell>, <verbatim|H_G>,
  <verbatim|\\rho_\\ell>, and <verbatim|Z_\\ell> mean respectively the site
  count, periodic four-torus, positively oriented links, plaquette action,
  probability Haar law, product Haar prior, and partition integral defined in
  the manuscript. RG scales <verbatim|q_j>, RG clock <verbatim|\\chi(k,i)>,
  weights <verbatim|w_i>, level outputs <verbatim|\\Phi_{N,i}>, and limiting
  kernels <verbatim|F_i> are local to the quoted flat-sector interface. In
  particular <verbatim|q_j> has not been identified with public mesh
  <verbatim|a_N>.

