  The manuscript gauge-invariance proof is newly organized in elementary
  matrix language. Its formal counterpart is also explicit in
  <verbatim|YM.Lattice.face_gauge> and <verbatim|YM.Wilson.energy_gauge>; the
  bridge <verbatim|YangMills.energy_eq> identifies the public and internal
  action sums. The public definition itself does not prove that an arbitrary
  insertion token is gauge invariant: the relevant condition is separately
  required by <verbatim|YangMills.WilsonRegularity.invariant>.

  The finite normalization argument is newly organized from compactness,
  continuity, positivity, and the integral formula. The internal proof is in
  <verbatim|YM.Wilson.partition_pos> and the probability-measure instance on
  <verbatim|YM.Wilson.law>; <verbatim|YangMills.law_eq> transports that law
  to the public definition. The manuscript does not cite the Lean proof as a
  mathematical reference.

  The flat-sector displayed bound is a faithful reorganization of
  <verbatim|YM.RG08.Flat.Quorum.approximates>; the frame bound and pointwise
  limit are its <verbatim|frames> and <verbatim|converges> fields. The actual
  supplier is produced by <verbatim|YM.RG08.Flat.entrance_gate>, after a
  compatible level, sufficient horizon, price system, delay and block-length
  floor are supplied. I inspected the statement and immediate proof body, but
  did not trace the theorem's imported proof infrastructure or independently
  derive the estimate. No claim is made here that the RowCost estimate is
  proved by this prose.

  <section|Literature and editorial decisions><label|literature-and-editorial-decisions>

  The shared literature directory contains only its README and the unrelated
  SU(2) simplicity note; no accepted lattice-construction result is available
  there. A targeted web search located Kenneth G. Wilson, \PConfinement of
  quarks,\Q <em|Physical Review D> 10 (1974), 2445\U2459, <hlink|DOI
  10.1103/PhysRevD.10.2445|https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.10.2445>. The APS
  result inspected was the abstract/metadata, not the full paper. It is
  therefore used only as historical context, and no theorem, continuum limit,
  or RG estimate is attributed to it. The elementary finite gauge-invariance
  and normalization arguments are proved directly in the manuscript.

  No source-specific nickname is used as a mathematical assertion. The public
  Wilson family is kept distinct from internal <verbatim|YM.Family>; the
  public mesh <verbatim|a_N> is kept distinct from the internal RG scale
  <verbatim|q_j>; and the public coupling <verbatim|\\beta_{N,p}> is kept
  distinct from the positive blocking penalty <verbatim|\\lambda_{\\rm ker}>.

  <section|Open obligations and limitations><label|open-obligations-and-limitations>

  <\enumerate>
    <item>Unpack <verbatim|RowCost>, <verbatim|clock>, the output map and the
    scale sequence enough to establish the quantitative estimate from its
    mathematical RG hypotheses.

    <item>Prove or cite the quadratic supplier
    <verbatim|YM.RG08.Gallery.Sworn>, dual supplier <verbatim|Aura.licensed>,
    and Redo/Yamen length and payment estimates, checking each hypothesis on
    the selected same <verbatim|Run>.

    <item>Prove the bridge from the RG trajectory and finite-volume
    insertions to the public smeared Wilson moments, including the correct
    scale conversion, uniformity, and mesh-then-volume order of limits.

    <item>The selected-run theorem alone does not state the public hierarchy.
    The detailed theorem <verbatim|YangMills.constructed> and its full
    dependencies need a separate exact proof map and mathematical exposition
    before they can support the advertised existence conclusion.

    <item>No fresh Lean build, axiom audit, LaTeX build/render, or
    independent review was run in this bounded draft. The finite proof is
    ordinary mathematics; source correspondence is based on inspection only.
    The required <verbatim|python3 scripts/check_blueprint.py> command was
    attempted and failed because the bounded output does not include the unit
    metadata file required by the checker. The permitted outputs for this
    session are only this evidence file and the LaTeX section. <verbatim|git
    diff --check> completed successfully.
  </enumerate>

  <section|Inspection and command evidence><label|inspection-and-command-evidence>

  Commands actually run in the isolated clone included:

  <\verbatim-code>
    pwd && git status --short && sed -n ... CONTRIBUTING.md
    docs/coordination.md docs/proof-standard.md

    cat docs/notation.md && cat blueprint/glossary.md && sed -n ...
    blueprint/background/README.md

    sed -n ... Lean/PublicWilson.lean Lean/WilsonBridge.lean
    Lean/YM/Independent/ConstructionRun.lean

    sed -n ... Lean/PublicTheory.lean Lean/YM/Source/Construction.lean
    Lean/YM/Extraction/LatticeFamily.lean

    sed -n ... Lean/YM/Wilson/Law.lean Lean/YM/Gauge/MatrixGroup.lean
    Lean/YM/Lattice/Faces.lean

    sed -n ... Lean/YM/Integration/ActualRunNativeComponentRecipe.lean
    Lean/YM/Integration/NativePreselectedPostnumericPeriodRun.lean

    sed -n ... Lean/YM/Integration/NativeComponentRecipe.lean
    Lean/YM/Integration/RG05Preconstruction/PeriodConstruction.lean

    sed -n ... Lean/YM/RG08/Flat/Entrance.lean
    Lean/YM/RG08/Aura/Publisher.lean Lean/YM/RG/History.lean

    rg -n '...' Lean/PublicTheory.lean Lean/YM/... (targeted declaration/path
    searches)
  </verbatim-code>

  The targeted primary-source search and result were described above. No full
  Lean tree was read. No Lean or LaTeX build was run. Commands in this record
  are representative descriptions of the actual bounded reads; exact shell
  history is available from the contributor session, but output logs were not
  saved.

